What's your favorite pet? Your least favorite?

MY FAVORITES:

1. Master mind flayer.
Advantages: enormously powerful attack, wields weapons, wears armor
and amulets, *and* can wake up Rodney/quest nemeses if you need him
to. Vulnerable to wands of death when they go wild. Check this out:

Status of Slurpee (chaotic):  Level 20  HP 160(160)  AC -26, tame,
fast.

Disadvantages: *non* pet master mind flayers. Oh, and they're stupid
enough to kill themselves slurping blue jellies.

2. Purple worm.
Advantages: easy to tame, can attain 400 HP / level on par with Rodney
by swallowing wraiths in VoTD.

Disadvantages: "The purple worm swallows the green slime! BUUUURP! The
purple worm turns into a green slime!" Adios 400 HP monster.

3. warhorse
Advantages: very strong, fast steed. Can kill a priest with your help.
Easily acquired.
Disadvantages: they eat carrots. :(

MY LEAST FAVORITE:

Any monster insufficiently buff to kill a shopkeeper isn't worth
keeping past early game, in my mind, but of those that *can* -

1. Lich.
If you hit a single level teleporter, that lich will go wild, and
Flopsy the 300 HP arch-lich with -20 AC will greet you when you least
expect it. Plus, their attack stinks.
2. Archon.
Yes, I know it's technically the best pet in the game. However,
requires a wish, goes wild as easily as a lich will, can't kill Rodney
without quaffing numerous potions of gain level, and still gets pwned
by w and t. I'd rather wish for a cockatrice corpse on Astral than a
figurine of an archon.
3. Green slime.
Need I say more?



